  "database": "rschema_0447",
  "nl_text": "The database schema named rschema_0447 consists of five tables: User, Financial_Document, Notification, System_Configuration, and Document_Management.\nThe User table is used to store user information, including Associated_Unit, Password, Phone_Number, Role, User_ID (as the primary key), and Username. Each field is a VARCHAR type and allows NULL values.\nThe Financial_Document table is used to store financial document information, including Attachment_Path, Document_Category, Document_Content, Document_ID (as the primary key), Document_Level, Document_Number, Document_Title, Issue_Date, Issuing_Unit, Remarks, and Validity_Status. All fields are VARCHAR type and allow NULL values.\nThe Notification table is used to store notification information, including Issue_Date, Notification_Content, Notification_ID (as the primary key), Notification_Status, Notification_Title, and User_ID. User_ID is a foreign key referencing the User table.\nThe System_Configuration table is used to store system configuration information, including Admin_ID, Configuration_ID (as the primary key), Data_Type, Database_Directory, File_Upload_Directory, and System_Name. Admin_ID is a foreign key referencing the User table.\nThe Document_Management table is used to manage document operations, including Admin_ID, Document_ID, Operation_Time, and Operation_Type. Both Admin_ID and Document_ID are foreign keys referencing the User and Financial_Document tables respectively. The combination of Admin_ID and Document_ID forms the primary key of this table.\nThis schema ensures data integrity by enforcing primary key and foreign key constraints. It also allows for referential integrity, as the foreign keys ensure that the referenced data exists in the referenced table.",
  "gold_question": "Requirements:\n1.User Information Management: Each registered user in the financial system has a unique user ID, username, password, phone number, associated unit, and role.\n2.Financial Document Management: Collect and organize financial systems, accounting treatment FAQs, accounting practice tips, and other materials. Each financial document includes the document title, document number, issuing unit, issue date, document category, document level, validity status, remarks, document content, and attachment path. Administrators can perform operations on the document, recording the operation time and type.\n3.Notification Management: Users can publish notifications. The content of the notification includes the notification content, issue date, and notification status.\n4.Web System Configuration: Administrators can perform operations such as adding, modifying, or deleting database content. The configuration records the system name, database directory, data type, and file upload directory.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0447.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0447\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `associated_unit` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `financial_document` (\n  `document_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `document_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `document_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `document_content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `document_category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `document_level` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `issuing_unit` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `issue_date` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `validity_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `attachment_path` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`document_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notification` (\n  `notification_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `notification_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notification_content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `issue_date` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notification_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`notification_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `system_configuration` (\n  `configuration_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `system_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `data_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `database_directory` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `file_upload_directory` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `admin_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`configuration_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `system_configuration_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`admin_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `document_management` (\n  `admin_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `document_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`admin_id`, `document_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `document_management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`admin_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `document_management_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`document_id`) REFERENCES `financial_document` (`document_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
